WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
Cut open a potato, and its cells
are packed with grains of starch:

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.650
the plant's energy store.

3
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.080
Every one of those cells sits
inside a wall of cellulose,

4
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.400
strong enough to stop it bursting.

5
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.360
Take either one apart, and
you find the same unit,

6
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.180
over and over: glucose.

7
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:22.160
So why can one feed you,
while the other builds a tree?

8
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.660
In this mission, you'll compare three
giant molecules made from glucose:

9
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.900
starch, glycogen and cellulose.

10
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.390
Then you'll test how the shape of a store
changes how fast an enzyme can release

11
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.780
its glucose.

12
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: explain why starch can
feed you while cellulose builds a tree.
